# Russian х, which is the phone Q: tools/russian/make-ruru.py says why.
#
# What a T in a phoneme annotation lays down, in place of English's th. It is
# the wrapper insert_eng_spr_phone called for th, ZZlprp_load__insert_2pt_s_
# 2_1_ZZstring34, with the code it inserts changed and nothing else.
rule ru_insert_x takes 3 from glob.obj
  bare
  raw push param 2
  raw push param 1
  raw push param 0
  raw call lpta_rpta_loadp arity 3 depth 3
  raw push imm 0
  raw push sym ru_ph_x
  raw push imm 1
  raw push imm 2
  raw push param 0
  raw call insert_2pt_s arity 5 depth 8
  raw popn 8
  raw alu negl none reg r0
  raw alu sbbl reg r0 reg r0
  raw alu negl none reg r0
  raw return reg r0
end

# Whether the phone about to be spoken is х, for the arm of eng_con_vals that
# hands it to ru_ph_x.
rule ru_test_x takes 1 from es_val.obj
  bare
  call test_string_s 2 1 sym ru_ph_x
end

# Whether the phone is th or х, for the rules that time a consonant, its
# transition and the syllable it starts: х is spoken as English's th was
# when it stood for it, so it is timed as th is.
rule ru_test_th_or_x takes 1 from es_val.obj
  bare
  call ZZtest_string_s_2_1_ZZstring34
  if answer is 0
    answer 0
  end
  call test_string_s 2 1 sym ru_ph_x
end
